-- Q4888: Income Taxes Advanced [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The tax rate in effect at the start of the fiscal year","The statutory federal tax rate applied to quarterly income only","The estimated annual effective rate on year-to-date ordinary income, with discrete items recognized currently","The actual effective rate computed on income earned through the interim date"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): ASC 740-270 requires entities to estimate the annual effective tax rate at each interim date and apply it to year-to-date ordinary income. Discrete items such as tax law changes are recognized entirely in the period they occur.
