  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Deseasonalized value equals actual sales divided by the seasonal index: $1,380,000 / 1.15 = $1,200,000. This strips the 15% holiday uplift to reveal the baseline quarterly run rate (ASC 205-10 trend analysis). The lower figure represents normalized demand absent seasonal effects.
Wrong (B): The $1,200,000 figure does not prove underperformance; it simply removes seasonality to show the underlying trend.
Wrong (C): Multiplying by the index would double-count the seasonal effect rather than removing it.
