  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Residual income equals net income minus an equity charge (invested equity multiplied by cost of equity), measuring the dollar amount earned above the minimum required return on capital (ASC 280-10 segment reporting). It identifies whether a division truly creates value beyond its capital cost.
Wrong (A): This describes return on equity (ROE), which is a ratio rather than a dollar measure of excess returns.
