-- Q7954: Financial Statement Analysis [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Prepare a projection, because bank submissions require hypothetical assumption scenarios","Prepare a projection, because limited-use distribution reduces the CPA''s liability exposure","Prepare a forecast, because it reflects expected conditions for general-use distribution","Prepare either format, because AICPA standards do not distinguish them for lending"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AT-C Section 305, a financial forecast presents expected results based on expected conditions and is appropriate for general-use distribution to third parties such as lenders. Since Eastbrook intends to present best-estimate results, a forecast is the correct format.
Wrong (A): Projections use hypothetical what-if assumptions and are restricted to limited-use parties, which would exclude a general bank submission.
Wrong (B): Choosing a projection solely to limit liability misapplies the distinction, which is based on assumption type, not distribution preference.
Wrong (D): AT-C Section 305 explicitly distinguishes forecasts from projections based on whether assumptions are expected or hypothetical.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 7954;

-- Q7962: Financial Statement Analysis [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Accept, because audit opinions can be issued on projections with stated assumptions","Accept, but restrict distribution of the projection to general-use parties only","Decline to audit; offer an examination, agreed-upon procedures, or compilation instead","Accept and issue a qualified opinion that discloses the hypothetical assumptions used"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AT-C Section 305, a CPA cannot issue an audit opinion on prospective financial statements because the forward-looking nature precludes the evidence-gathering required for an audit. The CPA may perform an examination, agreed-upon procedures, or compilation.
Wrong (A): Auditing standards do not extend to prospective financial information regardless of how clearly assumptions are stated.
Wrong (B): Projections are restricted to limited-use, not general-use, distribution under AT-C Section 305.
Wrong (D): A qualified audit opinion is not available for prospective statements; the issue is jurisdictional, not one of scope limitation.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 7962;

