-- Q12984: Prospective Analysis and Forecasting [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Holt''s method eliminates the smoothing constant, removing subjectivity from forecasting","Holt''s method adds a seasonal index parameter to capture recurring annual patterns","Simple exponential smoothing is unbiased for trending data, making the switch unnecessary","Holt''s method adds a trend parameter (beta) that models upward drift and prevents systematic lag"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Simple exponential smoothing assumes a stationary series and systematically lags behind trending data (FASB ASC 275-10 estimation guidance). Holt''s double exponential smoothing introduces a second parameter, beta, that separately smooths the trend component, allowing the forecast to track both level and direction.
Wrong (A): Holt''s method retains the alpha smoothing constant and adds beta; it does not eliminate subjectivity.
Wrong (B): Seasonal indices are added by Holt-Winters triple exponential smoothing, not Holt''s double method.
Wrong (C): Simple exponential smoothing is biased for trending data, producing persistent underprediction when sales rise steadily.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12984;

